-- title:
--   Round six, complex side: the recursive C-layer computes C^{⊗e}
-- statement:
--   For every round-six complex network $J$ (`Prop8IfaceH W T m h`) and every number of axes $e$, the operator computed by the recursive C-layer equals the $e$-fold tensor power of the basic $2\times 2$ operator $C$:
--
--   $$\mathrm{recOpH}(J, e) = C^{\otimes e}.$$
--
--   Widths $e$ that are not powers of $m$ are handled by splitting $e = m f + r$.
--
--   In Lean:
